@startuml snapshot-lifecycle-states
title Snapshot state machine (specs/offline-snapshots.md, ADR-0005)
state Absent
state Storing
state Present
state ServingOffline

[*] --> Absent : dir exists, no file
Absent --> Storing : successful network fetch\n(disk cache enabled)
Storing --> Present : tmp written + atomic rename
Storing --> Absent : any IO/serialize failure\n(best-effort — fetch still OK)
Present --> Present : successful fetch refreshes\n(rewrite, atomic)
Present --> ServingOffline : fetch fails, load(slug) OK
ServingOffline --> Present : next successful fetch refreshes
Present --> Absent : load fails (hostile or corrupt file)\ntreated as no snapshot
ServingOffline --> Absent : (only via external corruption)
Absent --> [*]

note bottom of Present
  Every arrow into Absent from a load is the total-load contract:
  a hostile file cannot crash or poison — it is just gone.
end note
@enduml
